  "reel": {
    "script": "Guanabara Bay in Rio has been struggling with oil spills for ages. It's been awful for marine life and local fishers. But here's a cool idea: using human hair to clean it up. Donated hair makes these barriers that soak up oil. They're even protecting mangroves. It's working, and it's a great way to use something that would just be thrown away. What other clever ways have you seen to help the planet?",
    "hook": "Human Hair to the Rescue",
